WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.160
Back in the early 2000s, Hayden Panettiere&nbsp;
was everywhere. From her role in the popular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.760
series Heroes to plum parts in rom-coms like&nbsp;
I Love You, Beth Cooper, she made her rounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:17.938
in Hollywood. For all that exposure, however,&nbsp;
Panettiere has largely faded from public view.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.520
Panettiere rose to mainstream prominence&nbsp;
by starring as Claire Bennet on Heroes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.240
For a while, the show was enormously&nbsp;
popular and uniquely headline-making,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.840
something of a predecessor to the ever-expanding&nbsp;
world of TV series we know today. Those who were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.534
around for its burst of success will&nbsp;
likely recall its infamous tagline,

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.113
"Save the cheerleader, save the world."

00:00:41.113 --> 00:00:45.360
Claire Bennet is this very cheerleader,&nbsp;
and was featured prominently in the show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.840
promotional campaigns. Claire has&nbsp;
the power of cellular regeneration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.680
which allows her to heal quickly&nbsp;
from injuries and become practically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:58.400
immortal. When she initially discovers her&nbsp;
powers, she's both curious and frightened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.559
and eventually realizes that her own fate&nbsp;
might be tied to that of the entire world.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.000
Heroes didn't just earn the public's&nbsp;
acclaim — critics initially responded to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.499
it with glowing praise as well. The first&nbsp;
season inspired widespread excitement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.179 --> 00:01:18.080
scoring multiple wins and nominations&nbsp;
from a wide variety of industry awards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:24.240
including the Golden Globes and the Emmys. But in&nbsp;
later seasons, Heroes' ratings took a tumble. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.200
began to feel as though the writers had no real&nbsp;
plan for giving the show a satisfying conclusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:35.120
and the narrative became increasingly ludicrous&nbsp;
and convoluted. Unfortunately for Panettiere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:40.560
Heroes has become remembered for its stellar&nbsp;
first season and not much else. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.839
the show was canceled on a low note, which very&nbsp;
well might have impacted Panettiere's career.

00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:50.880
When Panettiere started her career as a&nbsp;
child actor, she worked on soap operas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:56.960
television movies, and the occasional miniseries.&nbsp;
Disney came calling in the late 1990s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:03.040
leading to her roles as Dot in A Bug's&nbsp;
Life and Suri in Dinosaur. Soon after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.800
she landed a memorable role in the football hit&nbsp;
Remember The Titans. As she got older and made a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:15.440
name for herself on Heroes, Panettiere found swift&nbsp;
and dazzling success — but it came with a price.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.560
She quickly found that she was being typecast.&nbsp;
She had already played a talented ice skater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:25.840
and high school student in Ice Princess, and&nbsp;
now she was playing a cheerleader on Heroes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:30.160
She also starred as a cheerleader in both&nbsp;
Bring It On: All or Nothing and I Love You,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:36.240
Beth Cooper. A theme was developing, and&nbsp;
she wanted out. She told Contactmusic :

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:40.480
"If I don't get out of this category&nbsp;
pretty quickly, it will just get more and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.600
more difficult to be seen as anything besides a&nbsp;
cheerleader. [...] Like ... you get in a corset,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.058
it's hard to get out of a corset again."

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.840
As fans of Nashville know, Panettiere is&nbsp;
one heck of a talented singer. But somehow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.160
her real-world music career never really&nbsp;
got off the ground. Panettiere made her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.000
way down the early sections of the&nbsp;
Disney actress-to-pop star path,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.280
recording songs for several Disney movies&nbsp;
including Ice Princess and Cinderella III:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:13.200
A Twist in Time. She even started working on her&nbsp;
own album, releasing a single entitled "Wake Up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:19.200
Call" in 2008. But she wasn't happy with the music&nbsp;
that her record label was pushing her to sing, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:25.040
has since revealed her dissatisfaction with this&nbsp;
release. She said in an interview with Vulture:

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.800
"At that point I was a puppet,&nbsp;
basically. It wasn't me."

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.960
However, these unpleasant experiences in the music&nbsp;
industry have proved useful to her as an actress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:39.680
While playing Juliette, an aspiring singer&nbsp;
and one of the main roles on Nashville,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.360
Panettiere took her experiences&nbsp;
into account as her character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.200
was encouraged to record music&nbsp;
she was not passionate about.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.320
"When I read this script and&nbsp;
it became that for Juliette,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.760
I was like, I understand. I know what that is."

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.400
Though things ended positively in this regard,&nbsp;
she doesn't think she'll try to record another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.800
album in the future, as she feels that people&nbsp;
will conflate her music with her character.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:08.640
After having her daughter Kaya in December&nbsp;
2014, Panettiere found herself struggling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:13.920
with postpartum depression. She sought treatment&nbsp;
multiple times, ultimately checking into a Utah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:19.360
treatment center for support in May 2016. She&nbsp;
has repeatedly chosen to share her struggles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:23.680
as she believes greater openness about the&nbsp;
condition can help other women who suffer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.840
from the condition. In an interview&nbsp;
with Good Morning America, she said:

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.826
"It takes you a while and you feel off,&nbsp;
you don't feel like yourself. [...]&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.826 --> 00:04:36.800
Women are so resilient and that's&nbsp;
the incredible thing about them."

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.080
She went on to say:

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.640
"I think I'm all the stronger for it. I think I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.560
a better mom because of it because you&nbsp;
never take that connection for granted"

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.480
Today, Hayden's daughter Kaya lives with&nbsp;
her father, former boxer Wladimir Klitschko&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:55.520
in Ukraine. Naturally, she still wants to spend&nbsp;
as much time with her daughter as possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:00.240
so she travels to Ukraine whenever she gets&nbsp;
the chance. It's easy to imagine this might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.120
a big part of why Panettiere doesn't always&nbsp;
have the free time to commit to new roles.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:10.640
Although they've been separated for several years&nbsp;
now, Panettiere and Klitschko enjoy a genuinely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:16.480
amicable bond, and seek to set a positive&nbsp;
example for their daughter. She told Us Magazine:

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:20.000
"We're still respectful of each other,&nbsp;
and we still have that friendship with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.160
each other. [...] It's not a situation&nbsp;
that you find yourself in all that often,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:27.259
so it's a new one. But I think&nbsp;
we've done a really good job."

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.000
It may seem contradictory to say&nbsp;
that a celebrity like Panettiere is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.280
actually a very private person, but that's the&nbsp;
truth. Unlike so many highly visible stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:42.000
Panettiere makes a point of not making every&nbsp;
detail of her life public. While she does share&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.400
her struggles with fans when she's ready,&nbsp;
like her battle with postpartum depression,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.920
she rarely posts on Instagram or&nbsp;
Twitter. It's a far cry from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:55.520
ultra-connected world of many stars, who have&nbsp;
multiple feeds updating on an hourly basis.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:00.160
It seems that Panettiere chooses to stay&nbsp;
out of the public eye to the fullest extent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.480
she can these days — and it's not necessarily&nbsp;
because of a lack of opportunities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.720
While plenty of celebrities enjoy sharing&nbsp;
their day-to-day lives on social media,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.278
Panettiere has strong boundaries&nbsp;
when it comes to privacy.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:18.480
As Panettiere tried to move forward in her career&nbsp;
and break away from her "cheerleader" image,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:24.480
she took on a majorly controversial role. In 2011,&nbsp;
she starred as Amanda Knox, the college student&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:30.480
who was convicted of the murder of Meredith&nbsp;
Kercher, in Amanda Knox: Murder on Trial in Italy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:36.000
In the real world, Knox was eventually exonerated&nbsp;
when another man was identified as the murderer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.760
and has since spoken openly about her ordeal.&nbsp;
Kercher's family was unhappy with the contents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:46.400
of the film, especially because it depicts&nbsp;
a fictionalized version of Kercher's murder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:50.960
John Kercher, Meredith's father,&nbsp;
said in an interview with Time:

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:56.400
"It's so awful what these film people have done.&nbsp;
Your imagination runs riot as it is about what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:01.680
happened, but to actually see it like this is&nbsp;
very different and very distressing. I was told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:06.240
the original brief and synopsis of the film was&nbsp;
to take it up to the point of the killing but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:11.840
not actually show the killing itself. It's obvious&nbsp;
from these pictures they are showing the killing."

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.520
While Panettiere may have had good&nbsp;
intentions when she accepted the role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:20.358
it's clear that this film was deeply upsetting&nbsp;
for those who lived through these events.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:26.640
After she began working on Nashville, Panettiere&nbsp;
decided to pack up and move to the city for which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:31.360
the show is named. She purchased a home in&nbsp;
Nashville, and subsequently realized that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:36.560
she was much happier living there instead of&nbsp;
in New York City or Los Angeles. She felt like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:42.000
she could be more laid-back, and more true to&nbsp;
herself. Moreover, she told Southern Living that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:47.200
appreciated that her new neighbors seemed to value&nbsp;
the little things in life, allowing her to slow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:53.360
down and stop focusing on the non-stop hustle of&nbsp;
life in the entertainment industry. She continued:

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:57.280
"The people here are amazing. Living in&nbsp;
Nashville gives me a sense of normalcy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:01.760
that I wasn't sure I was ever going to get&nbsp;
back in my life. When I first got here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:06.560
all my defenses were still up, and I was&nbsp;
waiting for that world to suddenly creep back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:10.560
in. When it didn't, I realized that&nbsp;
I can live a normal life here with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:15.000
people who don't judge you based on what&nbsp;
you do or who you are in the public eye."

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:20.800
Recently, Panettiere has opened up about her&nbsp;
struggle to leave an abusive relationship.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:26.720
In the summer of 2020, her ex-boyfriend, Brian&nbsp;
Hickerson, was arrested on several charges of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:31.520
domestic abuse. Now, Panettiere is&nbsp;
speaking out about what happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:36.960
and why she hopes her story can help other&nbsp;
people who are in similar situations break free:

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:40.800
"I am coming forward with the truth about&nbsp;
what happened to me with the hope that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:45.360
my story will empower others in abusive&nbsp;
relationships to get the help they need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:51.199
and deserve. I am prepared to do my part to&nbsp;
make sure this man never hurts anyone again."

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:57.280
Now, she's focusing on herself and rebuilding&nbsp;
her life. For Panettiere, stepping away from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:02.080
camera for a while has been necessary: After&nbsp;
going through such a traumatic experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:07.840
she wants to put her health and wellbeing&nbsp;
first. Healing has to take priority. Happily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:12.758
she has found the courage to speak out and&nbsp;
has surrounded herself with supportive people.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.840
Panettiere is well-known for her activism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:20.240
particularly in regards to animal&nbsp;
welfare. After appearing on Heroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:24.960
she realized that she could use her new&nbsp;
platform for good. She told Teen Vogue:

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.040
"The show put me in a place to speak for&nbsp;
the things that I'm passionate about."

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:34.080
Panettiere joined up with the Whaleman&nbsp;
Foundation in 2007 to protest dolphin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:38.480
hunting. She was personally involved in a&nbsp;
confrontation between a group of fishermen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:43.520
and several surfers in Japan, who had&nbsp;
arrived to protest the annual dolphin hunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:50.000
in Taiji. This incident is explored in the 2009&nbsp;
documentary The Cove, which analyzes this annual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.800
dolphin hunt and offers viewers a call to&nbsp;
action for the welfare of these animals.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:59.440
Today, Panettiere still serves as a&nbsp;
spokesperson for the Whaleman Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:02.480
She told Conde Nast Traveler in an interview:

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:06.240
"I'm an activist who's aware of what's&nbsp;
realistic to achieve and what's not.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:10.400
The Whaleman Foundation's goals] are&nbsp;
achievable, and they make sense."

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:13.760
It goes without saying that this&nbsp;
level of devotion to a cause would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:18.400
hinder any actress' ability to remain&nbsp;
steadfast in Hollywood's spotlight.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:26.080
In 2018, the final episode of Nashville aired,&nbsp;
ending Panettiere's six year run as Juliette&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:31.520
Barnes. Since then, she has not appeared&nbsp;
in any other television shows or movies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:35.120
Currently, she does not have much&nbsp;
in the way of future roles lined up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:41.280
either. At this point, it looks like Panettiere&nbsp;
is purposefully enjoying a well-earned hiatus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:46.320
and that she does not have any immediate&nbsp;
plans to get back in front of the camera.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:51.280
Considering everything Panetierre has gone&nbsp;
through over the course of the past decade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:56.160
it's easy to see why she feels the need to&nbsp;
take some time off from acting. She's welcomed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:01.600
a daughter, battled postpartum depression,&nbsp;
and spoken out about abuse — that's enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:06.480
to push anyone to the brink. But she has&nbsp;
not made any statements about retiring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:11.440
meaning she'll likely be back on screen in&nbsp;
the future. In the meantime, fans of her work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:16.720
will be waiting to see what her next move is.&nbsp;
There's no denying her talent: When Panettiere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:22.960
does decide to act, sing, or campaign again,&nbsp;
she'll certainly enjoy a warm welcome back.

